<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Remarks">Remarks</span></h2>
<p>Relevant Eclipse engine code: 
&lt;cpp&gt;
</p>
<pre>   pEvent-&gt;SetType(CSSCRIPTEVENT_EVENTTYPE_RULES_APPLYEFFECT);
   pEvent-&gt;SetData(0, pEffect);
</pre>
<p>&lt;/cpp&gt;
</p><p>Use <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/GetCurrentEffect" title="GetCurrentEffect">GetCurrentEffect</a> to get the effect that was just applied (there is no <code>GetEventEffect</code> function) which can be decomposed to get the effect's creator, type, etc.
</p>
